Now let's see the Java shim interaction of Java renderer with C ABI? The Java HtmlRenderer is pure Java. It also has renderDebug, etc. Need add options.

Also inspect the design of DOM client navigation/title: when route changes, title updated by app signal via META, and browser URL via onRoute. For SEO, canonical should update? Client-side SPA canonical could be updated when route changes. Issue scope SSR only ("SEO-hardened SSR"), but canonical should likely also be kept in sync by DOM client via route hook? Hmm. The issue says "Make the server-rendered document fully crawlable and richly indexed". Canonical is a server concern. DOM client not required. But there's a "per view" hook; perhaps only SSR.

Let's examine how PathlandSession obtains Environment/route, and where metadata like base URL could be provided by host. PathlandRegistry.renderHtml(route, windowId) is called by controllers; easiest path: add overload `renderHtml(route, windowId, DocumentMeta meta)` or registry `renderHtml(route, windowId, requestBaseUrl)`; host computes canonical URL. But starter should automatically compute canonical from request and pass it. Also registry needs a metadata resolver hook to derive OG/Twitter from route/title. Let's think.

DocumentMetadata options struct in Java:
```java
public final class DocumentMetadata {
  String canonicalUrl;
  String imageUrl;
  String siteName;
  String ogType; // website/article
  String twitterCard; // summary_large_image
  String twitterSite;
  boolean jsonLd;
  ...
}
```
Then renderer overloads `render(frame, root, DocumentMetadata meta)` / `renderLinked(frame, root, cssBase, meta)`. Rust `DocumentMeta` struct with fields, and methods `render_document_with_meta` or builder `with_document_meta`. C ABI additions would be needed only if Java calls Rust via JNA; but Java is pure port. Still, for cross-language hosts Swift/.NET use the capi; to keep parity, maybe add a JSON options C ABI? This can get complex. The issue may be scoped to Rust SSR + TS DOM client + Java port (pure). The capi is used by other hosts though. Need decide how far.

Let's check AGENTS: "pathland-render-html ... C ABI (cdylib) ... Java uses pure-Java port". Tests GoldenConformance compare Java output to Rust fixtures. So any head changes require both implementations and update fixtures.

JSON-LD: "component-type-driven" suggests deriving JSON-LD from view components. What indexable content exists? Pages are arbitrary; generic structured data can be WebPage/WebSite (name, description, url, inLanguage) always. Article for ROLE_ARTICLE containers: headline from first heading text, description from first paragraph, image from first IMAGE src within, author/publisher unknown. BreadcrumbList from nav? Could be too speculative.

Maybe the intended design is simpler: emit JSON-LD `WebPage` with name/description/url/inLanguage, plus `Article` for each landmark article with headline/description/image. Let's search issue trackers maybe other references in docs/transcripts. Search repo for "json-ld" with case insensitive all files excluding node_modules, maybe transcripts.

